# Netlify: the files in the published folder that are not part of the site answer the not-found
# page: the hosts' own configurations (Cloudflare Pages' _routes.json, which scripts/build-web.mjs
# writes, among them), and metadata.json, which a plain `npx expo export` writes (the build
# removes it). `404!` rather than `404`: a plain rule is shadowed by a file at the same path, and
# these are files that can be there. Netlify never serves _headers or
# _redirects itself; they are listed so the three configurations refuse the same paths. Netlify
# reads this file from the published folder, so it covers that folder and nothing else: publish
# the folder the build writes, never the repository (only nginx, whose configuration lives
# outside the folder, also refuses a checkout published by mistake). Cloudflare Pages does not
# apply 404 rules, so `npm run build:web -- --host cloudflare` leaves this file out. Netlify runs
# no Function of this site, so its api/ is a 404 like any other missing path, and the page draws
# no sign-in and no shop.
/_headers        /404.html  404!
/_redirects      /404.html  404!
/.htaccess       /404.html  404!
/_routes.json    /404.html  404!
/metadata.json   /404.html  404!
